The advantages of daggers are simple: you don't have to unwield
your melee weapon to throw them (effectively), you don't
automatically loose some, and the +2 to hit.  The advantages of
arrows is a lot less weight, and more damage per projectile.
Depending on the character or the situation, one or the other
can predominate---a ranger who stumbles on three or four arrow
traps in the first level of the mines is likely to be better off
using arrows than daggers, and of course, in the late game, when
your luck is maxed out and you've blessed them (so losses are
minimal), and you're hitting at 100% anyway, arrows beat daggers
consistently, except if you're really meleeing most of the time,
and want to keep that melee weapon in hand.

(The one time I got as far as getting the amulet as a ranger, I
had well over 700 +7 blessed arrows, and was carrying 100 of
them around in open inventory without being burdened.  If I
hadn't choked on a Wraith corpse, I probably would have
ascended.  It was precisely the situation I just described: the
mines were full of arrow traps, and almost no daggers.)

